🥪 Delicious-sandwitch-capstone-2

📖 Project Overview

The Delicious Sandwich Shop Application is a fully object-oriented Java console application that simulates a real sandwich shop ordering system.

This capstone project demonstrates:

✅ Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
✅ Interfaces & Polymorphism
✅ Inheritance
✅ File Handling & Receipt Saving
✅ Input Validation
✅ Unit Testing with JUnit 5
✅ Professional Package Organization
✅ Git & GitHub Version Control

Customers can:

Create custom sandwiches
Add drinks and chips
Add toppings and sauces
Choose extra meat and extra cheese
Order specialty sandwiches
View order summaries
Generate receipt files automatically
✨ Features
🏠 Home Screen
Start a new order
Exit application
Menu input validation
🥪 Sandwich Customization

Customers can choose:

Bread type
Sandwich size
Toasted option
Meats
Extra meat
Cheeses
Extra cheese
Regular toppings
Sauces
🌟 Specialty Sandwiches

The application includes bonus specialty sandwiches using inheritance:

BLT
Philly Cheesesteak

These sandwiches automatically include preset ingredients and pricing.

💲 Dynamic Pricing

The application calculates pricing based on:

Sandwich size
Premium meats
Premium cheeses
Extra meat upgrades
Extra cheese upgrades
Drinks
Chips
🥤 Drinks

Customers can select:

Drink flavor
Drink size
🍟 Chips

Customers can add chips to any order.

🧾 Checkout System

The system:

Displays order summaries
Calculates total pricing
Confirms completed orders
💾 Receipt Saving

Orders are automatically saved as receipt text files.

Example:

20260527-153025.txt
✅ Input Validation

The application safely handles:

Invalid menu choices
Incorrect sandwich sizes
Invalid numeric input
Unsupported selections
🧪 Unit Testing

JUnit tests were created using the professional:

Arrange → Act → Assert

structure.

Unit tests include:

Sandwich pricing tests
Drink pricing tests
Chips pricing tests
Order total tests
Order summary tests
🧠 Object-Oriented Programming Concepts Used
📦 Classes & Objects

Custom classes include:

Sandwich
Drink
Chips
Order
Topping
ReceiptWriter
UserInterface
🔗 Interfaces

The OrderItem interface standardizes:

getPrice()
getSummary()

across all menu items.

🔄 Polymorphism

The Order class stores all items using:

ArrayList<OrderItem>

allowing multiple object types to behave through a shared interface.

🧬 Inheritance

Specialty sandwiches extend the Sandwich class:

Sandwich
   ↑
BLT
   ↑
PhillyCheeseSteak

This demonstrates reusable code and subclass behavior.

🔒 Encapsulation

Private fields and public methods are used throughout the application.

🗂 Modular Design

The project is separated into packages:

com.pluralsight
com.pluralsight.models
com.pluralsight.ui
com.pluralsight.util

